<title>BRAZIL: Brazil justice rejects gov't appeal on CVRD.</title>
<headline>Brazil justice rejects gov't appeal on CVRD.</headline>
<dateline>BRASILIA 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>A high court justice upheld his decision to suspend a federal land transfer to state mining giant Companhia Vale do Rio Doce (CVRD), which could delay next week's scheduled privatization of the company.</p>
<p>A spokesman for the Supreme Federal Tribunal, Brazil's highest court, said the government's appeal against the injunction would now be heard by a full meeting of the court later on Wednesday.  </p>
<p>The high court was also due to rule Wednesday on one of two constitutional challenges brought by a group of attorneys against the CVRD sale.</p>
<p>Brazil's National Development Bank (BNDES), which is managing the privatization of CVRD, said it would appeal all challenges to the sale. BNDES said the sale was still set for April 29.</p>
<p>((--William Schomberg, Brasilia newsroom, 5561-322-6962))</p>
